# Expected skill loads for the mkt-primitive-set brief (level: primitive, agent: design-builder), derived from the
# Routing table in design-craft/SKILL.md. evals/score.sh reads the first two fields of each line.
#   pass <skill>       a pass row of the part's level for the agent: PASSES needs a result for it.
#                      applied -> its text must come back; n/a -> its text must not come back.
#   must <skill>       a fired trigger or the Verify pass: its text must come back.
#   forbid <skill>     an unfired trigger, another agent's row, another level's row, or a skill out of the router.
#   allow <skill>      may come back; not required.
#   ambiguous <skill>  scored like allow; the routing table leaves the expectation open (see the reason).
#   open <word>        design runs only: the open part; the DECISION NEEDED block must name it.
# Every skill that comes back and is not pass (applied), must, allow or ambiguous is unexpected.

# Passes of the level.
pass better-colors                 # row: Primitive | Pass: palette, semantic tokens, contrast, dark mode | builder
pass better-typography             # row: Primitive | Pass: type scale, font loading, wrapping | builder
pass better-layout                 # row: Primitive | Pass: spacing, grouping, responsive, RTL | builder
pass better-ui                     # row: Primitive | Pass: radius, shadow, border, icons | builder
pass animate                       # row: Primitive | Pass: motion tokens and new animations | builder

# Fired triggers and the Verify row.
must design-qa                     # row: Verify | Pass: every part | both (every part)
must browser-checks                # row: Verify | Trigger: any browser step | both (the brief allows a browser)

# Ambiguous.
ambiguous interface-review         # row: Component | Pass: the part changed existing UI | builder. The token change restyles existing sections, but the row is Component level
ambiguous shadcn                   # row: Component | Trigger: the project uses shadcn (components.json) | builder. Fires in this fixture (components.json), but the row is Component level and Build step 3 loads the triggers of the part's level only
ambiguous copywriting              # row: Any | Trigger: marketing copy | both. The page holds marketing copy, but the primitive part changes no copy
ambiguous design-taste-frontend    # row: Product | Pass: which overall look and house rules? | both. surfaces/public-page.md sends every public-page part to its sections while it gathers facts; the row level is Product
ambiguous emil-design-eng          # row: Primitive | Trigger: a motion feel call | builder. DESIGN.md fixes durations and easing; whether applying them is "a motion feel call" is open
ambiguous stageshow                # row: Screen, flow | Trigger: a product illustration or demo on a page | both. Sort step 1 counts the demo slot as a second surface whose file loads it, but this part does not build the slot

# Unfired, other-level and other-agent rows, and skills out of the router.
forbid better-accessibility        # row: Component | Pass: custom controls, dialogs, focus, keyboard | builder (another level)
forbid better-writing              # row: Component | Pass: labels, errors, empty states, confirmations | builder (another level)
forbid state-machine               # row: Component | Pass: states, one at a time | both (another level)
forbid break-ui                    # row: Component | Pass: renders data: worst-case fixtures and fixes | builder (another level)
forbid review-animations           # row: Component | Pass: changed motion code | builder (another level)
forbid ask-sonner                  # row: Component | Trigger: toasts with sonner | builder (no sonner in package.json)
forbid coss                        # row: Component | Trigger: the project uses coss or Base UI | builder (components.json style radix-nova; radix-ui, no @base-ui/react)
forbid mobile-native               # row: Any | Trigger: phone users | both (DESIGN.md: no phone users)
forbid apple-design                # row: Primitive | Trigger: springs, gestures, drag, sheets | builder (DESIGN.md Motion: no springs, gestures, drag or sheets)
forbid laws-of-ux                  # row: Screen, flow | Pass: navigation, forms, multi-step flows, destructive actions | both (another level)
forbid better-interface            # row: Screen, flow | Pass: a review across domains | builder (another level)
forbid build-design                # row: Screen, flow | Trigger: a Figma file or a design image is the source | builder (DESIGN.md is the source)
forbid explain-interface           # row: Product | Pass: how was a site the owner names built? | design (design-only row)
forbid find-animation-opportunities # row: Screen, flow | Pass: what here should move? | design (design-only row)
forbid prototype                   # row: Screen, flow | Trigger: a state model or logic question is open | design (design-only row)
forbid improve-animations          # row: Screen, flow | Trigger: the owner asks to improve existing motion | design (design-only row)
forbid variant                     # row: Component | Pass: structure, density, emphasis, type or voice | design (design-only row)
forbid emil-prototype              # row: Component | Pass: motion or interaction feel, while it is open | design (design-only row)
forbid break                       # row: Component | Trigger: every scenario on one page, for one look | design (design-only row)
forbid pick-ui-library             # row: Component | Trigger: a new UI library is needed | design (design-only row)
forbid design-md                   # row: Product | Trigger: the project has no DESIGN.md (create), or the brief calls its direction weak (improve) | design (another agent's row; a builder with no DESIGN.md stops with DECISION NEEDED, D24)
forbid impeccable                  # out of router: spec D13
forbid grill-design                # out of router: spec D13
forbid agent-browser               # out of router: spec D13 (the skill stub; the CLI is used directly)
forbid make-interfaces-feel-better # out of router: spec D13
forbid animation-vocabulary        # out of router: spec D13
forbid hallmark                    # out of router: spec D13
forbid coss-particles              # out of router: spec D13
forbid build-design-library        # out of router: spec D4
forbid animate-expo                # out of router: spec D13 platform skill
forbid write-swift                 # out of router: spec D13 platform skill

allow design-craft                 # injected workflow (agent file inject-skills); a re-read is not a routed load
